.\" Manual page for rasterminal.
.\" Kept in sync by hand with src/args.cpp's --help text; update both together.
.\" The .TH version and date track src/version.h; bump them when cutting a release.
.TH RASTERMINAL 1 "2026-06-27" "rasterminal 0.1.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.\" ASCII fallbacks for the accented author name: groff's -Tascii table drops
.\" u00FD (y-acute) entirely, so without these the name renders "Ulicn" (a
.\" letter short). utf8/latin1 still use the real glyph where the device has it.
.\" mandoc ignores .fchar (groff extension) and substitutes its own ASCII
.\" transliteration, so the two "unsupported request" lint notices are expected.
.fchar \[u010D] c
.fchar \[u00FD] y
.SH NAME
rasterminal \- render a 3D model in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rasterminal
[\fIoptions\fR]
.I model
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rasterminal
renders 3D models in the terminal. It uses native-resolution kitty or sixel
images where supported and Unicode half-blocks elsewhere. The backend is
detected at startup and can be selected with
.BR \-\-graphics .
The
.B \-\-color
option controls 24-bit or 256-color text output.
.PP
The model operand is required. A lone
.B \-
is treated as a positional operand, not stdin.
.PP
Interactive mode requires terminals on standard input and standard output. If
either is piped or redirected,
.B rasterminal
exits without writing escape sequences. The headless
.B \-\-bench
mode works with redirected streams.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B .obj
Wavefront OBJ with optional .mtl (diffuse/specular/normal maps).
.TP
.B .ply
ASCII or binary (little- and big-endian).
.TP
.B .stl
ASCII or binary. Z\-up coordinates are remapped to Y\-up. ASCII lines are
limited to 64 KB.
.TP
.B .gltf, .glb
glTF 2.0 (PBR materials, textures, node transforms).
.TP
.B Other formats through Assimp
AMF, 3DS, AC, ASE, Assbin, B3D, BVH, Collada, DXF, CSM, HMP, IrrMesh,
IQM, IRR, LWO/LWS, MD2/MD3/MD5/MDC/MDL, NFF/NDO/OFF, Ogre, OpenGEX,
MS3D, COB, Blender, IFC, XGL, FBX, Q3D/Q3BSP, RAW, SIB, SMD, Terragen,
Unreal 3D, DirectX X, X3D, 3MF and MMD.
The Assimp loader imports static geometry and common materials and textures.
It flattens scene transforms and does not retain animation, skinning, cameras,
lights or format-specific metadata. OBJ, PLY, STL and glTF/GLB always use their
native loaders, including when parsing fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Initial state
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shading " " \fImode\fR
Initial shading mode:
.BR wireframe | flat | phong .
Default:
.BR phong .
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bg " " \fIcolor\fR
Initial background color:
.BR black | gray | white
.RB ( grey
also accepted). Default:
.BR black .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lighting " " \fImode\fR
Initial lighting mode:
.BR dual | single | flat .
Default:
.BR dual .
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wireframe\-color " " \fIcolor\fR
Initial wireframe edge color:
.BR white | red | green | yellow | cyan | magenta .
Default:
.BR white .
.TP
.BI \-\-yaw " DEG"
Initial camera yaw in degrees, in
.BR [\-180,\ 180] ;
positive turns the model left on screen, the direction selected by
.B \-\-spin\-direction
.BR left .
Also sets the
.B \-\-bench
camera. Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-pitch " DEG"
Initial camera pitch in degrees, in
.BR [\-180,\ 180] ;
negative looks down from above,
.B \-90
is top\-down, and values past \(+-90 view the model upside down. Under
.B \-\-first\-person
the value is clamped just inside straight up or down. Also sets the
.B \-\-bench
camera. Default:
.BR \-17.2 .
.TP
.BI \-\-zoom " FACTOR"
Initial zoom as an apparent\-size multiplier of the auto\-fit framing, in
.BR [0.2,\ 100] :
.B 2
appears twice as large and
.B 0.2
starts fully zoomed out. Under
.B \-\-first\-person
this sets the starting distance. Also sets the
.B \-\-bench
camera. Default:
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-first\-person\-speed " FACTOR"
Initial movement speed as a multiplier of the model\-scaled default, in
.BR [0.05,\ 20] ,
the range used by
.BR +/\- " and the wheel."
Requires
.BR \-\-first\-person .
Default:
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BR \-\-cull ", " \-\-no\-cull
Enable or disable backface culling initially; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-cull .
.TP
.BR \-\-texture ", " \-\-no\-texture
Enable or disable texture rendering initially; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-texture .
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-spin ", " \-\-no\-spin
Enable or disable auto-rotation initially; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-no\-spin .
.SS Runtime and load
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " " [\fIN\fR]
Worker threads. Bare
.B \-j
uses all cores;
.BI \-j " N"
uses
.IR N ,
clamped to the CPU thread count. The default depends on the backend: all cores
under
.BR kitty " and " sixel ,
and
.B min(cores,4)
under blocks. Model loading always uses all cores.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fps " " [\fIN\fR]
Frame cap. Bare
.B \-f
is uncapped;
.BI \-f " N"
caps at
.I N
fps. Default:
.BR 30 .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-bench " " [\fIN\fR]
Headless benchmark: run
.I N
frames (default
.BR 200 )
after warmup, report timing, fps and throughput to standard error, then exit.
The benchmark performs no terminal I/O.
.TP
.BI \-\-bench\-size " WxH"
Bench framebuffer size in pixels (default
.BR 200x120 ).
Requires
.BR \-\-bench .
.TP
.BI \-\-bench\-warmup " N"
Bench warmup frames discarded (default
.BR 20 ;
.B 0
for none). Requires
.BR \-\-bench .
.TP
.BI \-\-smooth\-angle " DEG"
Crease angle in degrees, in
.BR [0,\ 180] ,
used to compute missing normals. Adjacent faces smooth below the angle and form
a hard edge above it. Default
.BR 60 ;
.B 0
is faceted,
.B 180
is fully smooth. Ignored when an OBJ authors smoothing groups.
Assimp-backed formats cap this setting at Assimp's 175-degree maximum.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " mode"
Color output:
.B truecolor
and its alias
.B 24bit
force 24-bit output,
.B 256
forces 256-color output, and
.B auto
detects the terminal from the environment. The default is
.BR auto .
See
.B ENVIRONMENT
for the detection order.
Forcing a color mode does not bypass the
.B TERM=dumb
rejection or the Windows VT-capability gate.
Kitty images remain 24-bit and sixel images use 240 colors, so this option
affects only the HUD under those backends.
.TP
.BI \-\-graphics " mode"
Rendering backend.
.B kitty
draws real pixels through the kitty graphics protocol,
.B sixel
draws real pixels through sixel graphics,
.B blocks
draws Unicode half-block cells, and
.B auto
prefers kitty, then sixel, then blocks. The default is
.BR auto .
.IP
A sixel image uses the 240-color xterm palette at native resolution. It uses
whole 6-pixel bands and leaves the last terminal row clear to prevent scrolling,
even under
.BR \-\-no\-hud .
It honors the terminal's advertised image limit and centers a limited image when
the cell size is known. xterm defaults to 1000x1000 pixels and discards larger
images. Its
.B maxStringParse
resource defaults to 600000 and drops larger sixel payloads. Raise it with
.BR "xterm \-xrm '*maxStringParse: 10000000'" .
.IP
Forcing
.B kitty
or
.B sixel
requires successful detection. Both modes are unavailable under tmux and GNU
screen.
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-speed " DEG/S"
Auto-rotation speed in degrees per second. It applies to
.B \-\-spin
and the Space toggle. The value must be positive. Use
.B \-\-spin\-direction
to select direction.
Default
.BR 45 .
.TP
.BI \-\-spin\-direction " dir"
Auto-rotation direction:
.B left
or
.BR right ,
the way the model's front face moves on screen. Default
.BR left .
.SS Session-fixed toggles
.TP
.BR \-\-ao ", " \-\-no\-ao
Enable or disable baked ambient occlusion; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-ao .
.TP
.BR \-\-hud ", " \-\-no\-hud
Show or hide the HUD status line; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-hud .
.TP
.BR \-\-input ", " \-\-no\-input
Enable or disable the keyboard and mouse controls; the later flag wins. Default:
.BR \-\-input .
Under
.B \-\-no\-input
every binding in
.B CONTROLS
is ignored except
.BR Q ,
which still quits, as does Ctrl+C. Input is still read and cannot accumulate in
the terminal. The viewer keeps mouse tracking active, so dragging does not
select text. Auto-rotation, terminal resizing and
.B \-\-bench
are unaffected.
.TP
.BR \-\-first\-person ", " \-\-no\-first\-person
Use a free\-flying first\-person camera instead of the turntable; the later flag
wins. Default:
.BR \-\-no\-first\-person .
The camera has no gravity or collision and can pass through geometry.
WASD moves, the arrows and a mouse drag look,
.BR E " and " V
move along world up, and
.BR +/\- " and the wheel"
set movement speed. Speed scales with model size. Pitch stops at straight up or
down, and distance is limited to the orbit zoom range. Auto\-rotation turns the
view from the camera's current position. The launch pose comes from
.BR \-\-yaw ", " \-\-pitch " and " \-\-zoom .
.B \-\-bench
ignores this mode.
.PP
.B \-\-spin\-direction
describes model movement in turntable mode and view movement under
.B \-\-first\-person
mode.
.SS Meta
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and license information and exit.
.SH OPTION SYNTAX
A long flag accepts its value after a space or
.RB ' = ' .
For example,
.B \-\-shading flat
and
.B \-\-shading=flat
are equivalent. Short flags accept a space or compact form, as in
.B \-s flat
and
.BR \-sflat .
String values are case-insensitive.
.PP
Boolean flags take no value:
.B \-\-cull=on
is an error, not a synonym for
.BR \-\-cull .
For paired flags such as
.B \-\-cull
and
.BR \-\-no\-cull ,
the later one wins.
.PP
No-argument short options may be clustered behind one
.RB ' \- '
with at most one value-taking option last.
For example,
.B \-Sj4
means
.BR \-S " " \-j4 .
A bare
.B \-\-
terminates option parsing. Every following token is the model operand, even one
beginning with
.RB ' \- '.
.SH CONTROLS
While rendering:
.TP
.B 1\-3
Select shading mode.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle spin.
.TP
.B WASD, arrows, mouse drag
Orbit the camera.
.TP
.B +/\-, scroll
Zoom.
.TP
.B B
Cycle background.
.TP
.B L
Cycle lighting.
.TP
.B R
Reset the camera and runtime settings to the command-line state, or to their
defaults when no state flags were passed.
.TP
.B C
Cycle wireframe color.
.TP
.B K
Toggle backface culling.
.TP
.B T
Toggle textures.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.PP
Under
.B \-\-first\-person
the camera bindings change: WASD moves instead of orbiting, the arrows and a
mouse drag look,
.BR E " and " V
move up and down, and
.BR +/\- " and the wheel"
set the movement speed instead of zooming. Everything else in the list is
unchanged.
.PP
Under
.B \-\-no\-input
none of the above act except
.BR Q " and " Ctrl+C .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including
.BR \-\-help " and " \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, model load failure, or a terminal
.B rasterminal
cannot draw to outside
.BR \-\-bench .
Terminal errors include redirected input or output,
.B TERM
is
.BR dumb ,
a Windows console cannot enable ANSI escapes, or a forced
.B \-\-graphics kitty
or
.B \-\-graphics sixel
backend is not detected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B rasterminal
reads these variables in interactive mode to choose color output and detect
terminal multiplexers. The headless
.B \-\-bench
mode reads none of them.
.PP
With
.BR "\-\-color auto" ,
the first matching rule wins:
.B TERM=dumb
is rejected; GNU screen uses 256 colors;
.B COLORTERM
truecolor hints select 24-bit output; recognized
.B TERM
hints and terminal names select 24-bit output; everything else uses 256 colors.
Native Windows consoles default to 24-bit when neither variable identifies a
mode.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
selects 24-bit output except inside GNU screen.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
is always rejected. A
.B \-direct
terminfo name, a name containing
.B truecolor
or
.BR 24bit ,
or a known truecolor terminal name selects 24-bit output. Recognized terminals
are kitty, WezTerm, Alacritty, Ghostty, foot and Contour. This also preserves
24-bit output over SSH, which does not forward
.BR COLORTERM .
.TP
.B TMUX
A non-empty value exempts a screen-family
.B TERM
from the GNU screen floor, unless
.B STY
marks a screen session. The graphics query is skipped whenever
.B TMUX
is set, even to an empty value, or
.B TERM
starts with screen or tmux. Under a multiplexer,
.B \-\-graphics auto
uses half-blocks and a forced pixel backend is an error.
.TP
.B STY
A non-empty value marks GNU screen and forces the 256-color default.
.PP
.B \-\-color
overrides color detection but not the
.B TERM=dumb
rejection.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Render a model with default settings:
.B rasterminal model.glb
.TP
Start in wireframe with a white background, spinning:
.B rasterminal \-s wireframe \-b white \-S model.obj
.TP
Benchmark 500 frames headlessly at a fixed size:
.B rasterminal \-\-bench 500 \-\-bench\-size 400x240 model.stl
